//Optimal - discuss below algorithm if additional space can be utilized
/**
Time: O(n) average
Space: O(n)
 */
class Solution {
    public boolean containsDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        HashSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
        for(int i: nums){
            if(!set.add(i))
                return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}

/**
input = [1,2,3,1]
set.add(1) = true
set.add(2) = true
set.add(3) = true
set.add(1) = false

HashSet.add() returns:
true → element was not already present, so it was added.
false → element already existed.
 */
==================================
//no additional space, but input is modified by sorting
//Sorting — O(n log n) time, O(1) auxiliary space
public boolean containsDuplicate(int[] nums) {
    Arrays.sort(nums);

    for (int i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
        if (nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) {
            return true;
        }
    }

    return false;
}
===============
| Approach    |          Time |               Space | 
| ----------- | ------------: | ------------------: | 
| Brute force |         O(n²) |                O(1) | 
| Sorting     |    O(n log n) | Low auxiliary space | 
| **HashSet** | **O(n) avg.** |            **O(n)** | 
